        "title": "Fiber Preparation: Scouring, Carding, Combing, Retting",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Raw fiber from animal or plant is contaminated with oils, waxes, plant matter, dirt, and other impurities. Preparation removes these to give clean, aligned fiber ready for spinning. The preparation method also determines the character of the resulting yarn: carded fiber (random alignment) makes soft, airy woolen yarn; combed fiber (parallel alignment) makes smooth, strong worsted yarn."
    },
